course: dictionary
lesson: 5215
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word «jay» is one of them. The sentences around it tell you which meaning is right.
explain: A jay is a noisy, colourful bird. «Jays bury thousands of acorns each autumn to eat in winter.» The words acorns, autumn and winter tell you this is the bird.
explain: «Jay» can also be the letter J, or a name like Jay in your class. Ask yourself: does this sentence make sense with a bird, a letter or a person in it?
fact: A jay is a noisy, colourful bird of the crow family.
fact: The Eurasian jay is pinkish brown with bright blue wing patches. The blue jay of North America is blue and white.
fact: Jays bury acorns to eat in winter. The ones they forget can grow into new oak trees, so jays help plant forests.
fact: A jay's loud screech warns other animals of danger.
fact: «Jay» is also the letter J, and Jay is a name.
exercise: «Jays bury thousands of acorns each autumn to eat in winter.» What is a jay in this sentence? | A person called Jay | A type of oak tree | The letter J | *A noisy, colourful bird
exercise: Ella writes, «Jay starts with J.» What does jay mean here? | A name for a friend | *The letter J | A blue feather | A noisy bird
exercise: «Forgotten acorns can grow into oak trees.» Which bird does this sentence probably describe? | A robin with a red breast | A parrot | *A jay | A penguin
test: Why do jays bury acorns in autumn? | To keep warm in summer | To eat in winter | To make the acorns ripen faster this week | *To eat in winter, and some forgotten acorns grow into trees
test: «Jay is my best friend at school.» What does jay mean here? | The letter J | A bird with blue wings | *A name for a person | A type of tree
exam: «The loud jay screeched to warn the others of a cat.» What does jay mean here? | *A noisy bird that warns others of danger | A name for a boy | The letter J | A tree that grows acorns
